  "id": "modeling-theory",
  "term": "modeling theory",
  "definition": "Modeling theory is the use of formal mathematical models to represent how an epidemic spreads and ends, and to test explanations such as whether transmission is limited by the number of susceptible people. In this context, it also highlights that the assumptions built into a model can strongly shape the conclusions drawn from observed data.",
